; ted-readline-tab-overflow (#378): readline expands a TAB before it
; checks the end of the line buffer charbuff2; with a tab size above 133
; (only from L:blitzeditor.opts) the blanks run past the end of TED's
; buffer block (2438 bytes, charbuff3 is its last 130 bytes).  blitz2
; under inject pad (64 zeroed bytes behind every allocation, checked when
; it is freed), tab size 300, a text file "a<TAB>b"; QUIT (TED frees its
; buffer block).  Correct: nothing is written behind the block; the
; original writes blanks behind it (inject: "written behind").
; @file bo.bas "a\tb\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @opts tabstop=300
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject pad blitz2:blitz2 @FILE@
; @expect nostdout "inject: pad: written behind an allocation of 2438 bytes"
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
